by `strlen`, so no replacement | [ ] |\n| 18 | `find_and_replace_char` | long valid NUL-terminated string | [ ] |\n| 19 | `validate_and_normalize` | value negative, including `INT_MIN`; returned unchanged | [ ] |\n| 20 | `validate_and_normalize` | value zero; returned unchanged | [ ] |\n| 21 | `validate_and_normalize` | positive value `1..63`; clamped to octal `0100` (64) | [ ] |\n| 22 | `validate_and_normalize` | value exactly octal `0100` (64) | [ ] |\n| 23 | `validate_and_normalize` | value `65..510`; returned unchanged | [ ] |\n| 24 | `validate_and_normalize` | value exactly octal `0777` (511) | [ ] |\n| 25 | `validate_and_normalize` | value `512..INT_MAX`; clamped to octal `0777` (511) | [ ] |\n| 26 | `findrep` | fresh state; zero active parameters, no add/multiply call, accumulator inactive | [ ] |\n| 27 | `findrep` | fresh state; one active parameter in position 1 or 2, add runs and accumulator becomes active | [ ] |\n| 28 | `findrep` | fresh state; one active parameter only in position 3 or 4, add runs with two zero operands and accumulator stays inactive | [ ] |\n| 29 | `findrep` | fresh state; at least two active parameters, multiply runs; `p3 * p4 == 0` | [ ] |\n| 30 | `findrep` | fresh state; at least two active parameters, nonzero multiplier `<=` octal `0100`; divide branch not taken | [ ] |\n| 31 | `findrep` | fresh state; at least two active parameters, multiplier `>` octal `0100`; post-result divide branch taken | [ ] |\n| 32 | `findrep` | normalized `p1 + p2 >` octal `0150`; subtract branch taken | [ ] |\n| 33 | `findrep` | accumulator nonzero and multiplier nonzero; both-active contribution taken | [ ] |\n| 34 | `findrep` | accumulator zero or multiplier zero; both-active contribution skipped | [ ] |\n| 35 | `findrep` | each parameter position traverses negative, zero, low-positive clamp, in-range, and high-positive clamp classes | [ ] |\n| 36 | low-level mutators then `findrep` | preloaded positive/negative/zero accumulator and multiplier plus non